  {
   "id": "n03",
   "text": "Ninjas: *the black outfit myth.*",
   "frames": 77
  },
  {
   "id": "n04",
   "text": "Real ninjas, called *shinobi,* were spies.",
   "frames": 116
  },
  {
   "id": "n05",
   "text": "A spy's job is to *blend in.*",
   "frames": 95
  },
  {
   "id": "n06",
   "text": "So they dressed like *everyone else.*",
   "frames": 88
  },
  {
   "id": "n07",
   "text": "Farmers. Merchants. *Monks.*",
   "frames": 88
  },
  {
   "id": "n08",
   "text": "A black suit in daylight? *Very suspicious.*",
   "frames": 107
  },
  {
   "id": "n09",
   "text": "So where did the black *come from?*",
   "frames": 77
  },
  {
   "id": "n10",
   "text": "From *the theatre.*",
   "frames": 66
  },
  {
   "id": "n11",
   "text": "In kabuki, the stage crew dressed all in *black.*",
   "frames": 125
  },
  {
   "id": "n12",
   "text": "The audience pretended they were *invisible.*",
   "frames": 105
  },
  {
   "id": "n13",
   "text": "So when a ninja appeared on *stage...*",
   "frames": 97
  },
  {
   "id": "n14",
   "text": "...dressing them like the stage crew was the *perfect trick.*",
   "frames": 125
  },
  {
   "id": "n15",
   "text": "Prints and movies *copied the look.*",
   "frames": 91
  },
  {
   "id": "n16",
   "text": "And now every ninja wears *black.*",
   "frames": 99
  },
  {
   "id": "n17",
   "text": "Real shinobi? Hard to spot. *That was the point.*",
